<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>NAS Backups Privacy Policy</title>
</head>
<body>
  <h1>NAS Backups Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p>Last updated 17 November 2026</p>

  <h2>Purpose</h2>
  <p>
    NAS Backups is a private application used by Dirk Bouma to
    automatically back up files from his personal NAS to his
    personal Google Drive account.
  </p>

  <h2>Google Drive access</h2>
  <p>
    The application requests the Google Drive drive.file permission.
    This allows it to create, read, update, and delete files and
    folders created by the application or explicitly authorized
    for use with it.
  </p>

  <h2>Data use and storage</h2>
  <p>
    Google Drive access is used to upload backup files, check
    backup contents and metadata, restore files, and manage
    backup retention. Backup data is stored on the personal NAS
    and in the connected Google Drive account.
  </p>
  <p>
    Authorization credentials are stored on the NAS so scheduled
    backups can run automatically. Google authorization is
    handled through Google's sign-in process.
  </p>

  <h2>Sharing</h2>
  <p>
    Backup contents are transferred to Google Drive for storage.
    The application does not sell Google user data or use it
    for advertising. Backups are intended for the account
    owner's personal use.
  </p>

  <h2>Retention and deletion</h2>
  <p>
    Backups are retained according to the owner's configured
    retention settings and may be deleted manually.
    The owner can revoke the application's access through
    Google Account settings. Revoking access stops future
    access but does not delete existing backups.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    For questions, contact
    <a href="mailto:boumadirk2007@gmail.com">
      boumadirk2007@gmail.com
    </a>.
  </p>

  <p><a href="./">Return to homepage</a></p>
</body>
</html>
